  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-19 (independent auditor, after 40a03eb762 and db457cb3c2). Section 9.1: \"Implementations MUST support all lexical representations specified in this document.\" Tagged units are unchanged; the cited producers changed. db457cb3c2 splits compound guards in readInstancePredicates and readEqualsQuoted into one guard per operand with identical bodies, no behavior change. 40a03eb762 makes instanceExists a referenceWalk method that compares a leaf-list predicate value with sameValue (canonicalValue of both sides under the leaf-list's type) and selects a list entry through the canonical keyIndex (canonicalKey) instead of the raw map-key address, so a configured value and a default in use now answer the same lexical forms. This resolves the prior judgement's observation that [.='+17'] matched a default 17 but not a configured 17 (Section 9.1: \"In particular, any XPath expression evaluations are done using the canonical form if the data type has a canonical form.\"). The '.' leaf-list-predicate parse, *WSP handling and absent-value refusal that TestRFC7950InstanceIdentifierLeafListPredicate and ...Absent assert are unaffected (string leaf-list: canonicalValue is identity), and the integer, decimal64, binary, bits, leafref and union-default units of the prior judgement stand. All tagged units and TestReferenceCanonicalValueRefusesOther pass at HEAD (go test -tags 'ze_core ze_bgp' over config/yang and config). The canonical comparison is proven by TestRFC7950InstanceIdentifierCanonicalValue under RFC7950-9.13-1, not by a 9.1-1 tag.",
